{"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","modules":[{"name":"ScreenStates"}],"role":"article","title":"Accessibility"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A placeholder is often the ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"only","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" thing on screen for a few hundred milliseconds, or the only thing a user with a slow connection sees for much longer than that — so it’s worth it being as accessible as the real content it stands in for. The default ","type":"text"},{"code":"ScreenStateDefault{Empty,Loading,Error}View","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"code":"UIView","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"s handle all of this out of the box; this article rounds up what they do and how a fully custom placeholder can match them.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"VoiceOver-announcements","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"VoiceOver announcements"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Each default placeholder announces its own appearance — ","type":"text"},{"code":"AccessibilityNotification.Announcement(_:).post()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in SwiftUI, ","type":"text"},{"code":"UIAccessibility.post(notification:.announcement, argument:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in UIKit — so a screen settling into ","type":"text"},{"code":".empty","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":".loading","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", or ","type":"text"},{"code":".error","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is heard, not just seen.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState\/accessibilityAnnouncement","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" exposes that same wording for any case, so a fully custom placeholder can announce transitions consistently instead of inventing its own text:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":[".onAppear {","    if let announcement = state.accessibilityAnnouncement {","        AccessibilityNotification.Announcement(announcement).post()","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"It’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for ","type":"text"},{"code":".data","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — your own content is what VoiceOver should read at that point — and, for ","type":"text"},{"code":".empty","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", it’s the default “Nothing Here” text; announce your own custom title directly instead if your placeholder shows one, so VoiceOver matches what’s on screen. See ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithSwiftUI","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithUIKit","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" for the full examples.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Reduce-Motion","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Reduce Motion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The default Loading placeholder’s ring spins via a repeating rotation animation — purely decorative, and exactly the kind of large, continuous motion Reduce Motion exists to suppress. ","type":"text"},{"code":"ScreenStateDefaultLoadingView","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" reads SwiftUI’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"accessibilityReduceMotion","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" environment value; ","type":"text"},{"code":"ScreenStateDefaultLoadingUIView","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" reads ","type":"text"},{"code":"UIAccessibility.isReduceMotionEnabled","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and also observes ","type":"text"},{"code":"UIAccessibility.reduceMotionStatusDidChangeNotification","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so an already-visible spinner responds immediately if the setting changes while on screen, not just on the next appearance. Either way, the ring stays static — still colorful, just not spinning — instead of disabling itself entirely, since a static ring still communicates “loading” on its own.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Increase-Contrast","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Increase Contrast"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"All three default placeholders’ gradient icons\/ring respect Increase Contrast — SwiftUI’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"colorSchemeContrast","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" environment value, UIKit’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"UIAccessibility.isDarkerSystemColorsEnabled","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (observed live the same way Reduce Motion is). A multi-stop gradient can dip below an acceptable contrast ratio in places a single flat color never does, so when Increase Contrast is on, every gradient is swapped for a solid ","type":"text"},{"code":".label","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"code":".primary","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" tint instead.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Dynamic-Type","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Dynamic Type"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The default Empty\/Error placeholders’ text scales with Dynamic Type: SwiftUI’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"ScreenStateDefaultEmptyView","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"code":"ErrorView","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" get this for free from ","type":"text"},{"code":"ContentUnavailableView","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"’s own text styles, and ","type":"text"},{"code":"ScreenStateDefaultEmptyUIView","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"code":"ErrorUIView","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"’s labels use ","type":"text"},{"code":"UIFont.preferredFont(forTextStyle: .body, compatibleWith:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Both are covered up to the largest accessibility size by snapshot tests, so a regression that silently pins the text to a fixed size would be caught. The default Loading placeholder has no text at all — its ring is a fixed-size shape, unaffected by Dynamic Type by design.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Identifiers-for-XCUITest","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Identifiers for XCUITest"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Every default placeholder exposes a stable ","type":"text"},{"code":"accessibilityIdentifier","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", independent of any localized or custom text, so a UI test can assert which state is showing without string-matching:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"table","header":"row","rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Identifier","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Shown on","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"screenStates.loading","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateDefaultLoadingView","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateDefaultLoadingUIView","isActive":true,"type":"reference"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"screenStates.empty","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateDefaultEmptyView","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateDefaultEmptyUIView","isActive":true,"type":"reference"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"screenStates.error","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateDefaultErrorView","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateDefaultErrorUIView","isActive":true,"type":"reference"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"screenStates.error.retryButton","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The Retry button, when ","type":"text"},{"code":"onRetry","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is given","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"screenStates.error.secondaryActionButton","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The secondary action button, when ","type":"text"},{"code":"secondaryAction","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is given","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]]}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/screenstates\/accessibility"]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/Accessibility","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates"]]},"sections":[],"kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Everything the default placeholders — and your own custom ones — get for free: VoiceOver, Reduce Motion, Increase Contrast, Dynamic Type, and stable identifiers for XCUITest."}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Related-Documentation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithSwiftUI","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithUIKit"],"title":"Related Documentation"}],"references":{"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/ScreenStateDefaultEmptyUIView":{"type":"topic","title":"ScreenStateDefaultEmptyUIView","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ScreenStateDefaultEmptyUIView"}],"url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/screenstatedefaultemptyuiview","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"ide